  "uses_raw": true,
  "prompt": "Which subscription events arrived more than once? These tables may hold errors. Some subscription events arrived twice: two rows of subscription_events are copies of one event when subscription_id, event_type, event_date and mrr_delta_local all match. Keep the row with the lowest event_id. Clean nothing else. For each event with more than one row, return five columns, in this order: kept_event_id (the event_id of the row kept), subscription_id, event_type, event_date and copies, the number of rows that arrived for that event. Return one row for each such event. Any row order is fine.",
